INT. PLUMLEY'S CLOCK REPAIR - BACK WORKROOM - DAY

Forty ticking clocks, none agreeing. HORACE PLUMLEY, 60s, bow tie, loupe on his eye, bends over a gutted grandfather clock.

CHESTER VOSS, 50s, a rival dealer in a camel coat, tiptoes in by the rear door. WINNIFRED, 60s, Horace's sister, sets down a tea tray.

CHESTER
(low)
Horace, old friend. I'll give you five hundred for the Lindqvist clock.

HORACE
It's not for sale.

CHESTER
Everything is.

He reaches for the clock. Horace grabs the pendulum. Chester grabs the other end. They tug, nose to nose.

WINNIFRED
Gentlemen!

Both men freeze. The pendulum swings between them and clangs a bell. They let go, then both lunge for the clock again and topple into a heap on the floor.

HORACE
He started it!

WINNIFRED
He did not. He's sitting on your hat.

Chester pulls the hat from under him and offers it with a weak smile. Horace snatches it. Winnifred pours tea into three cups and hands one down to each of them.

WINNIFRED (CONT'D)
Now. Five hundred?

HORACE
(sighs)
Make it six.
